<!-- hardcalc 1 -->

# Budget 2026

An example of the hardcalc format. This file is valid Markdown.

```types
Euro   = decimal(2) unit "€"
Status = enum(open, paid, cancelled)
```

```functions
gross(x) = x * 1.19   # gross amount with 19 % VAT
share(part; total) = part / total
```

## Expenses :: matrix[*, 5]

| Item | Amount:Euro | Status:Status | Share:decimal(3) | Gross:Euro |
|---|--:|---|---|---|
| Rent | 1200.00 | paid | =B1/sum(B) | =Amount |
| Power | 85.50 | open | =B2/sum(B) | =Amount * 1.19 |
| Internet | 39.99 | paid | =B3/sum(B) | =Amount * 119% |

```layer format
B: align right
D: percent(1)
row[Status=open]: fg yellow
```

```layer validate
B: >= 0
Item: required unique
```

```layer comments
B1: Rent increase announced for July
```

```chart Spending
type:   bar
data:   Expenses!Amount, Expenses!Gross
labels: Expenses!Item
```

Rent is **{=Expenses[Rent, Share] | percent(1)}** of the expenses,
the gross total is {=sum(Expenses!Gross)}.

## Sales :: tensor[Month, Region, Product]

| Month | Region | Product | Value:Euro |
|---|---|---|---|
| Jan | North | A | 120.00 |
| Jan | South | A | 80.00 |
| Feb | North | A | 135.00 |
| Feb | South | B | 42.10 |

```chart SalesTrend
type:   line
data:   Sales
x:      Month
series: Region
filter: Product=A
```

## Metrics :: vector

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Total expenses | =sum(Expenses!Gross) |
| Rent | =Expenses[Rent, Amount] |
| Sales North | =sum(Sales[Region=North]) |
| Result | =B3 - B1 |
| Distance | =12 * Speed |
| Speed | 5 m/s |
| Trend | =spark(Expenses!Gross) |

A plain Markdown table is an anonymous matrix:

| x | y |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |

```layout Report
page: A4 portrait
font: 9
grid: 12
1-12 / 1-2    heading  Budget 2026
1-6  / 4-12   table    Expenses   columns: Item, Amount, Share
7-12 / 4-12   chart    Spending
1-8  / 14-16  text     Rent is **{=Expenses[Rent, Share] | percent(1)}** of the expenses.
9-12 / 14-16  value    sum(Expenses!Gross)   label: Total expenses
1-12 / 18-19  note     All figures are provisional.
```
